@* SPEC:  docs/00-COMPONENTS/2.8/03-LipiPagination-Spec.md §8.6 (StyleGuide standalone demo) *@
@* PHASE: 2.8 Data Display — Stage 7 (LipiPagination demo) — CHANGE-LOG A50, A50.1 (visual styles) *@
@* DEMO:  lives in LiPi.Web (not redistributable) per packaging rule. *@
@page "/admin/style-guide/data-display/pagination"
@layout LiPi.Web.Components.Layouts.TopNavLayout
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using LiPi.Components.DataDisplay
@using LiPicons.Blazor

<PageTitle>LipiPagination — StyleGuide</PageTitle>

<div class="sg-page">
    <header class="sg-header">
        <h1>LipiPagination</h1>
        <p>Page-navigation for LipiTable / LipiList — three variants (Full, Compact, Minimal),
           a page-size selector, a row-count readout, optional jump-to-page, and a separate
           Load-more sub-component. Composes LipiSelect + LipiButton; all-LiPi package surface,
           zero native controls. The page-number window is the AntDesign/Material rule
           (boundary pages + sibling window + ellipsis), verified against the LP-14 test set.</p>
    </header>

    @* ── Section 1: Full variant (live) ──────────────────────────────────── *@
    <section class="sg-section">
        <h2>Full variant</h2>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            The complete bar: page-size selector + row-count readout + first/prev + page numbers
            + next/last. Bound to live state — click through and watch the window, ellipsis, and
            readout update. <code>TotalCount=487</code>, default <code>Siblings=1</code>,
            <code>BoundaryCount=1</code>.
        </p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_fullPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_fullSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full" />
        <p class="sg-readout">
            <strong>Page</strong> @_fullPage &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Page size</strong> @_fullSize
        </p>

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">Full + jump-to-page + wider window (Siblings=2)</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            <code>ShowJumpToPage="true"</code> adds an opt-in "go to page" input (Full only).
            <code>Siblings="2"</code> widens the window to 5 centred pages so the ellipsis sits
            further out.
        </p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_jumpPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_jumpSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full"
                        Siblings="2"
                        ShowJumpToPage="true" />
        <p class="sg-readout">
            <strong>Page</strong> @_jumpPage &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Page size</strong> @_jumpSize
        </p>
    </section>

    @* ── Section 1.5: Visual styles (A50.1 — CellStyle / ActiveStyle / ChevronStyle) ── *@
    <section class="sg-section">
        <h2>Visual styles</h2>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            Three independent style axes, all token-overridable. <code>CellStyle</code>
            (<code>Bordered</code> / <code>Borderless</code>) sets the page-number affordance;
            <code>ActiveStyle</code> (<code>Solid</code> / <code>Tint</code>) sets how the current
            page is signalled; <code>ChevronStyle</code> (<code>Auto</code> / <code>Bordered</code> /
            <code>Ghost</code>) controls the nav arrows and defaults to following
            <code>CellStyle</code>. The zero-config default is
            <code>CellStyle=Bordered</code> + <code>ActiveStyle=Solid</code>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">Bordered grid + Solid active (default)</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">The out-of-the-box look — a bordered button grid with a solid-fill
            active page. Chevrons follow the grid (bordered) via <code>ChevronStyle=Auto</code>.</p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_vsBsPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_vsBsSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full"
                        CellStyle="PaginationCellStyle.Bordered"
                        ActiveStyle="PaginationActiveStyle.Solid" />

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">Bordered grid + Tint active</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">Bordered cells, but the active page is a soft primary tint with a
            primary-colored number; the active cell is ringed in primary so it still reads among
            the bordered cells.</p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_vsBtPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_vsBtSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full"
                        CellStyle="PaginationCellStyle.Bordered"
                        ActiveStyle="PaginationActiveStyle.Tint" />

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">Borderless + Solid active</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">Page numbers are plain text; only the active page is filled
            (solid primary). Chevrons follow as ghost via <code>ChevronStyle=Auto</code>.</p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_vsLsPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_vsLsSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full"
                        CellStyle="PaginationCellStyle.Borderless"
                        ActiveStyle="PaginationActiveStyle.Solid" />

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">Borderless + Tint active (clinical)</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">The quietest look — borderless numbers, active page a soft primary
            tint. This is the recommended in-app HIS setting.</p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_vsLtPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_vsLtSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full"
                        CellStyle="PaginationCellStyle.Borderless"
                        ActiveStyle="PaginationActiveStyle.Tint" />

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">ChevronStyle override</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">Chevrons need not match the grid. Here a borderless number set keeps
            <code>ChevronStyle=Bordered</code> so the arrows stay framed while the numbers don't.</p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_vsCvPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_vsCvSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full"
                        CellStyle="PaginationCellStyle.Borderless"
                        ActiveStyle="PaginationActiveStyle.Solid"
                        ChevronStyle="PaginationChevronStyle.Bordered" />
    </section>

    @* ── Section 2: Compact variant ──────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <section class="sg-section">
        <h2>Compact variant</h2>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            Prev / "Page X of Y" indicator / Next — for tighter toolbars and side panels.
            No page-number strip, no page-size selector by default.
        </p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_compactPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_compactSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Compact" />
        <p class="sg-readout">
            <strong>Page</strong> @_compactPage &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Page size</strong> @_compactSize
        </p>
    </section>

    @* ── Section 3: Minimal variant ──────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <section class="sg-section">
        <h2>Minimal variant</h2>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            Just prev / next icon buttons — for cards, mobile, and dense embeds where the
            chrome must disappear. First/last and the page strip are intentionally absent.
        </p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_minimalPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_minimalSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Minimal" />
        <p class="sg-readout">
            <strong>Page</strong> @_minimalPage &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Page size</strong> @_minimalSize
        </p>
    </section>

    @* ── Section 4: Edge cases ───────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <section class="sg-section">
        <h2>Edge cases</h2>

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">Few pages (all fit — no ellipsis)</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            <code>TotalCount=38</code> at 10/page → 4 pages. Below the all-fit threshold, so every
            page renders contiguously with no ellipsis.
        </p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="38"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_fewPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_fewSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full" />
        <p class="sg-readout"><strong>Page</strong> @_fewPage &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Page size</strong> @_fewSize</p>

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">Empty (no rows)</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            <code>TotalCount=0</code> → the row-count reads "No items" and navigation collapses to a
            single inert page.
        </p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="0"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_emptyPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_emptySize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full" />

        <h3 class="sg-subhead">Disabled</h3>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            <code>Disabled="true"</code> — the whole bar is inert (e.g. while a page is loading).
        </p>
        <LipiPagination TotalCount="487"
                        @bind-CurrentPage="_disabledPage"
                        @bind-PageSize="_disabledSize"
                        Variant="PaginationVariant.Full"
                        Disabled="true" />
    </section>

    @* ── Section 5: Load-more (separate sub-component) ───────────────────── *@
    <section class="sg-section">
        <h2>Load more</h2>
        <p class="sg-note-p">
            <code>LipiPaginationLoadMore</code> is a distinct paradigm from paged navigation — an
            append-on-demand button, not a variant. It shows a remaining-count hint and hides itself
            once everything is loaded. Here a click loads 25 more of 487.
        </p>
        <LipiPaginationLoadMore LoadedCount="_loaded"
                                TotalCount="487"
                                IsLoading="_loadingMore"
                                OnLoadMoreClicked="OnLoadMore" />
        <p class="sg-readout"><strong>Loaded</strong> @_loaded <strong>of</strong> 487</p>
    </section>

    @* ── A11y notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <section class="sg-section">
        <h2>Accessibility</h2>
        <ul class="sg-notes">
            <li>The nav region carries <code>role="navigation"</code> + an <code>aria-label</code> (defaults to "Pagination").</li>
            <li>The active page button is marked <code>aria-current="page"</code>.</li>
            <li>The row-count readout is an <code>aria-live="polite"</code> region so screen readers hear range changes.</li>
            <li>Ellipsis is presentational (<code>aria-hidden</code>); it is never a focus target.</li>
            <li>First / Prev / Next / Last are real LipiButtons — full keyboard + focus-ring support, disabled at the ends.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    // Full variant
    private int _fullPage = 1;
    private int _fullSize = 25;

    // Full + jump + wide window
    private int _jumpPage = 8;
    private int _jumpSize = 25;

    // Visual styles (A50.1) — one state pair per demo so they page independently
    private int _vsBsPage = 1;  private int _vsBsSize = 25;   // Bordered + Solid (default)
    private int _vsBtPage = 3;  private int _vsBtSize = 25;   // Bordered + Tint
    private int _vsLsPage = 1;  private int _vsLsSize = 25;   // Borderless + Solid
    private int _vsLtPage = 3;  private int _vsLtSize = 25;   // Borderless + Tint
    private int _vsCvPage = 1;  private int _vsCvSize = 25;   // Chevron override

    // Compact
    private int _compactPage = 1;
    private int _compactSize = 25;

    // Minimal
    private int _minimalPage = 1;
    private int _minimalSize = 25;

    // Edge: few pages
    private int _fewPage = 1;
    private int _fewSize = 10;

    // Edge: empty
    private int _emptyPage = 1;
    private int _emptySize = 25;

    // Edge: disabled
    private int _disabledPage = 3;
    private int _disabledSize = 25;

    // Load more
    private int _loaded = 25;
    private bool _loadingMore;

    private async Task OnLoadMore()
    {
        _loadingMore = true;
        StateHasChanged();              // show the spinner before the await
        await Task.Delay(600);          // simulate a fetch
        _loaded = Math.Min(_loaded + 25, 487);
        _loadingMore = false;
    }
}
